[Music]  each of these pins is a Bed Bath and  Beyond that closed in 2022 that's about  20 of its stores Shares are at their  lowest point since the 90s after the  company said it's facing bankruptcy  bankruptcy bankruptcy as sales collapsed  Bed Bath and Beyond scrambled to cut  costs by laying off workers and closing  those stores here's what happened to the  Home Goods chain in the last six months  that led to a cash crisis and a  potential bankruptcy filing  let's turn back the clock to June when  Bed Bath and Beyond CEO Mark Trenton had  a problem his strategy of scaling back  coupons and doing away with popular  National brands in favor of private  labels was failing these are some of my  favorites from The Haven line and the  company was struggling to stock shelves  since it had fallen behind on payments  to vendors sales had fallen by 25  compared to the previous year and net  losses were up to over 350 million  dollars  on June 29th the company announced a  leadership change Sue Gove has been  named interim chief executive officer  replacing Mark Tritton who is leaving  the company at the time Gove said that  bed bath and Beyonds results are not up  to our expectations nor are they  reflective of our potential it was not  entirely surprising because the company  had reported a string of poor earnings  and falling sales and so it was well  known that the company was struggling in  August cash reserves key for paying  vendors were still low the company  needed more cash and was looking for a  loan to make that happen on the 23rd Bed  Bath and Beyond announced it had secured  500 million dollars in funding which it  hoped would help keep shelves stocked  some vendors had not been paid in months  and clearly the company was struggling  while the loan could pay for more  inventory it wasn't enough to keep every  store open Bed Bath and Beyond announced  it'd be closing 150 locations about 20  percent of its stores plus it would be  starting layoffs that amounted to a  fifth of its corporate and supply chain  staff  just two days later the company suffered  a different kind of loss CFO Gustavo  Arnold died by Suicide  at a time when a company is struggling  financially to lose your CFO that like  that is you know is certainly a shock  and it certainly made things even more  difficult for them when second quarter  earnings were released at the end of  September analysts said the company was  facing yet another cash crunch the 500  million dollar loan had weakened Bed  Bath and Beyond's balance sheet with  liabilities exceeding assets  still the company felt confident that  our current liquidity will enable the  necessary strategic plans we have  implemented but a few weeks later Bed  Bath and Beyond announced it'd be making  a debt exchange offer where a company  exchanges bonds for secured notes to  extend maturities and reduce interest  expenses the company was offering higher  interest rates in exchange for investors  taking a haircut on their principal it  meant note holders would lose money but  they'd be guaranteed something stock  prices dipped then fell more after gov  hosted a summit with suppliers at the  company's New Jersey headquarters to ask  for support she had several challenges  one players some of them had not been  paid in months and two the company had  pushed out some of these suppliers to  make way for its private label Brands  now it wanted the suppliers to come back  well these suppliers had found other  channels to sell their goods so it was  taking a lot of convincing to get the  suppliers back on board and I'm not sure  they were entirely successful these  vendor woes were all happening before  the busiest time of the year for  retailers the holiday season Bed Bath  and Beyond was still struggling to stock  shelves just a few days before black  Friday reports came out that more than  40 percent of the retailers products had  been out of stock in October some  suppliers said they were still owed  money and would pause shipments until  they were paid if you had empty shelves  you're not going to have people coming  in and buying and then you're not going  to have sales and it becomes a vicious  cycle sales didn't meet expectations  during the fourth quarter and on January  5th Bed Bath and Beyond announced it was  preparing to file for bankruptcy in just  a few weeks a spokeswoman for Bed Bath  and Beyond said it hadn't made any final  decisions and Gove said on the third  quarter earnings call we are committed  to to updating all stakeholders of our  plans as they develop and finalize in  that earnings report the company said  sales fell 33 percent and losses Rose to  393 million dollars our business was  built around our loyal customers  listening and responding to their  preferences was at the center veering  away from that path has led to our  recent financial performance the company  also said it is planning more layoffs in  an effort to cut costs bankruptcy is  still not a certainty but their ability  to avoid it is shrinking you know there  were things they could have done such as  sell their Buy Buy Baby chain for cash  and they chose not to do that so their  options are narrowing news of an  official bankruptcy filing could come in  the next few weeks  [Music]

